      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Outpatient endometrial biopsy was followed by delayed abdominal discomfort in 50% of cases. The pain started 2-3 h after the procedure, lasted for about 2 h and was described in most cases as similar to dysmenorrhoea of a moderate degree. Appropriate explanation and the use of a simple analgesic may reduce the discomfort and the anxiety with which it is associated."},
